From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeavesMC <noreply@leavesmc.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Optimize powered rail updates

Replaces the recursive power propagation of powered/activator rails with a
network-based search that visits each rail at most once per update and caches
the result per block-change epoch.

This patch is Powered by RailOptimization(https://github.com/EasterGhost/RailOptimization)

This patch is based on the following mixins:
* "RailOptimization/mixin/PoweredRailBlockMixin.java"
* "RailOptimization/mixin/BaseRailBlockMixin.java"
* "RailOptimization/mixin/LevelChunkMixin.java"
* "RailOptimization/mixin/LevelMixin.java"
* "RailOptimization/mixin/BlockStateMixin.java"
By: EasterGhost
As part of: RailOptimization (https://github.com/EasterGhost/RailOptimization)
Licensed under: GPL-3.0 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html)

Two behaviours are deliberately preserved from Paper's own version of
updateState: the BlockRedstoneEvent is still fired by the fallback path, and
the bridge performs the same binary redstone change notification itself when
it takes the fast path.

